## Brookhollow

dialogue-intro-1 = Brookhollow, a quiet village at the southern edge of the kingdom of Aldmere.
dialogue-intro-2 = Today's the day. I'm going to Valcrest to join the Adventurers' Guild... and one day I'll be the strongest hero in the world!
dialogue-intro-3 = Ha! Then start by surviving the road. Wolves keep coming down from the hills. Take these potions.
dialogue-intro-4 = Thanks, Elder Maren. Just watch me!

dialogue-elder-farm-1 = The Carvel farm, west of the fields, has wolves at its fences every night.
dialogue-elder-farm-2 = A hero helps the people in front of him before chasing glory, Taren.

dialogue-elder-later-1 = The Carvels can't stop talking about you! Valcrest lies north, past Thornwood Forest. Mind the goblins.

dialogue-farm-thanks-1 = You chased them off! My family owes you, lad.
dialogue-farm-thanks-2 = Just practice for the strongest hero in the world.
dialogue-farm-thanks-3 = Then the strongest hero needs better than a tunic. Here, my old leather vest. Go on, take it.

## Thornwood

dialogue-meet-lyra-1 = Arrows whistle through the trees. A young woman in a scout's coat stands among broken branches.
dialogue-meet-lyra-2 = Don't just stand there! Are you with them?
dialogue-meet-lyra-3 = With the goblins? I'm Taren of Brookhollow, future strongest hero in the world.
dialogue-meet-lyra-4 = ...Right. Lyra, scout of the Valcrest Guard. I was sent to find out why the goblins grew so bold, and I lost their trail in this cursed forest.
dialogue-meet-lyra-5 = Then let's find it together. Heroes help people, right?
dialogue-meet-lyra-6 = Fine. But I give the orders. Here they come!
dialogue-meet-lyra-7 = Lyra joins the party.

dialogue-lyra-insists-1 = The goblin camp is west of the fork. I'm not going back to Valcrest empty-handed.
dialogue-lyra-insists-2 = Then let's give them a reason to remember us.

dialogue-after-grukk-1 = Grukk falls. Behind his throne lie crates of new steel blades, each stamped with a black seal.
dialogue-after-grukk-2 = Goblins don't forge steel like this. Someone is arming them.
dialogue-after-grukk-3 = Someone in Valcrest?
dialogue-after-grukk-4 = Sergeant Holt needs to see this. The north gate, let's go.

## Valcrest

dialogue-arrive-valcrest-1 = Valcrest, capital of Aldmere. Its white walls rise above the northern road.
dialogue-arrive-valcrest-2 = The Adventurers' Guild is somewhere in here!
dialogue-arrive-valcrest-3 = Report first, Guild later. The guard post is past the plaza.

dialogue-guild-register-1 = Welcome to the Adventurers' Guild. New face? Name and ambition, please.
dialogue-guild-register-2 = Taren. I'm going to be the strongest hero in the world.
dialogue-guild-register-3 = Rank F, then. Everyone starts somewhere. Here's a welcome kit.

dialogue-guild-later-1 = Rank F, Taren. You climb by taking on real work, and the Guard has plenty.

dialogue-holt-report-1 = Lyra! We'd given you up for lost. And who's this?
dialogue-holt-report-2 = Taren of Brookhollow. He helped me bring down the goblin chief, Grukk. Sir, they carried these.
dialogue-holt-report-3 = That seal... these blades vanished from a shipment that never left the city. Someone inside Valcrest is supplying them.
dialogue-holt-report-4 = And the patrols report movement in the old catacombs beneath the city. The dead haven't stayed down lately.
dialogue-holt-report-5 = Then we'll go down there.
dialogue-holt-report-6 = You've earned the coin, and the chance. The catacomb gate is open to you. Don't make me write to your families.

dialogue-holt-catacombs-1 = The catacomb gate is past the guard post. Find out who is behind this.

## Catacombs

dialogue-enter-catacombs-1 = Cold air rises from the stairs. Somewhere below, bones scrape against stone.
dialogue-enter-catacombs-2 = Stay close. Skeletons hate fire... a pity neither of us casts it.
dialogue-enter-catacombs-3 = Then we hit harder.

dialogue-free-corin-1 = Behind rusted bars, a young man in a torn acolyte's robe looks up.
dialogue-free-corin-2 = Living people! Please, the key is on the jailer's belt.
dialogue-free-corin-3 = Got it. Who are you?
dialogue-free-corin-4 = Corin, acolyte of the Temple of Valcrest. I came down to bless the dead and found someone waking them instead. They locked me up when I saw his face.
dialogue-free-corin-5 = Whose face?
dialogue-free-corin-6 = The Warden's. He waits below. Let me come with you; my prayers can mend your wounds.
dialogue-free-corin-7 = Corin joins the party. His prayer heals everyone.

dialogue-after-warden-1 = The Warden crumbles to dust. Among his bones lies a letter sealed in black wax: a crown of thorns.
dialogue-after-warden-2 = "The tithe of steel is paid. Raise the dead and wait for my word." He was only following orders.
dialogue-after-warden-3 = Then whoever wrote this is still out there. Holt has to see it.
dialogue-after-warden-4 = There's a hidden stair over there. It must lead back to the city.

dialogue-holt-ending-1 = You came back, all three of you, and the catacombs are quiet.
dialogue-holt-ending-2 = The Warden was only a servant. He carried the same black seal, and this letter, signed with a crown of thorns.
dialogue-holt-ending-3 = A crown of thorns... I'll take this to the captain. The Guard owes you, and so does the Guild. Taren, I'd say that's rank E.
dialogue-holt-ending-4 = One step closer to the strongest hero in the world.
dialogue-holt-ending-5 = End of the first chapter. To be continued...

dialogue-holt-after-1 = Rest while you can. Whoever wears that crown of thorns will move again.
